Spec: LibSecretDockerconfigjson

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Decode a Kubernetes `kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson` Secret into `{user, pass}` for a
    given registry, so other scripts (Harbor/GitLab source scanners) can authenticate with
    credentials that live on-cluster rather than in argv.

Exposes:
  @get_auth_from(secret, namespace, registry) — the module's sole @fn; reached by importers
    as `secret::get_auth_from(...)` (the `import "secret_dockerconfigjson" as secret`
    convention frozen across ./scan_harbor.sdd and ./scan_gitlab.sdd). Returns a
    @#{user, pass} map of decoded strings.

Accepts:
  @secret — @String Secret name, read in @namespace.
  @namespace — @String namespace owning the Secret.
  @registry — @String registry host; MUST equal the exact key under `.auths` (no trailing
    slash, no `https://` prefix — it is a plain map index, not a match).

Returns:
  @#{user: <before-first-colon>, pass: <after-first-colon>} map. Field order is a literal
    map-literal at the return site.

Raises:
  @throw (Rhai error) whenever any step below is unsatisfied — these all surface as an
    interpreter error, not a typed result, because the file mints no guard of its own:
      - `k8s_resource("Secret", namespace).get(secret)` finds nothing (engine raises) or
        the Secret has no `.data[".dockerconfigjson"]`.
      - @base64_decode / @json_decode fail on the payload, or `.auths` is absent.
      - @auths[registry] is missing (no such registry key).
      - `.auth` is absent or not `user:pass` text.
  Split semantics: @auth.split(":") then @auth[0]/@auth[1] — a password containing `:`
    truncates to the first colon segment; a token with no second element makes @auth[1]
    an out-of-range index error. (See Tasks.)

Handles:
  Nothing defensively: zero `if`, zero `try/catch`, zero `.contains()` guards in these 6
    lines. Every failure mode is delegated to the engine raising.

Must:
  Read the secret through the engine primitive @k8s_resource("Secret", ns).get(name) —
    the raw-K8s lane frozen in the vynil-core `k8sraw` registrar (the script-side twin of
    ./../../common/src/k8sraw.sdd), NOT a typed instance getter.
  Decode exactly: @base64_decode(JSON-string) -> @json_decode -> @.auths registry key ->
    @base64_decode -> @.split(":") -> positional `[0]`/`[1]`. No `.docker` compat object,
    no email/identity handling, no `auths{}` c-plaintext branch (spec-dockercfg legacy
    form is NOT accepted).
  Keep the map-literal key names `user` and `pass` — importers index `auth.user` /
    `auth.pass`.

Depends on:
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — @k8s_resource(...).@get, @base64_decode, @json_decode
    (script surface; the Rust owners are the `k8sraw`/`json` registrars behind
    ./../../common/src/rhaihandler.sdd).
  ./scan_harbor.rhai + ./scan_gitlab.rhai — the two importers whose credential contract
    this must keep: `spec.pull_secret` secret name + `namespace` + exact registry host.

Scenario: exact registry key resolves
  Given a Secret whose `.dockerconfigjson` decodes to `auths` containing the key `harbor.example`
    with `auth` = base64("robot$pull:secretpart1:part2")
  When @get_auth_from("the-secret", "ns", "harbor.example") runs
  Then it returns `#{user: "robot$pull", pass: "secretpart1"}` — the split is on the FIRST
    colon and the remainder after the extra colon is dropped (see Tasks)
  And no error is thrown

Scenario: registry host not present
  Given the same Secret
  When @get_auth_from is called with registry `other.example`
  Then the interpreter raises (map index miss) rather than returning an empty credential

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide whether the first-colon split is correct for docker registries — a real
      docker `auth` is `user:pass`, but the code drops everything after the SECOND colon
      too via the `[0]`/`[1]` index pair; freeze whether truncation of colon-bearing
      passwords is intended or the split must be `split_once`.
  [ ] Decide whether a missing/empty `.auth` should raise or return empty creds like the
      kubectl-vynil resolver does (`("basic", ":")` posture in
      ./../../kubectl-vynil/src/actions.sdd scan lane) — the two credential decoders are
      deliberately different today.
  [ ] Add a mock-engine test: no `#[cfg(test)]` / `agent/tests` case drives this fn on the
      mock k8s; nearest coverage is via @list_repository indirectly (./scan_harbor.sdd).

Done when:
  A mock-k8s test covers the exact-key hit, the colon-split posture is recorded, and both
    importer contracts still hold.
